from pathlib import Path
import re,html,difflib,markdown,json
O=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;R=O.parents[3]
def render(s):return markdown.markdown(re.sub(r'<!--\s*@[^>]*-->','',s),extensions=['extra','sane_lists'])
def image(n,c):return '<figure><a href="'+n+'.png"><img loading="lazy" src="'+n+'.png" alt="'+html.escape(c,quote=True)+'"></a><figcaption>'+c+'</figcaption></figure>'
before=(O/'Color_Walls.before.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8');after=(R/'commons/maps/Color_Walls/final.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
assert after==(O/'Color_Walls.after.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
revision=json.loads((O/'revision.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
css=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',(O.parent/'2026-09-23-array-molnar-volume/index.html').read_text(encoding='utf-8'),re.S)[1]
page='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Walls — the view and the passage</title><style>'+css+'</style></head><body><main>'
page+='''<div class="eyebrow">Ada Research · Colour · 23 September 2026</div><h1>The view and the passage.</h1><p class="intro">The chair disappears.<br>The doorway stays where it was.</p><p class="status">Applied to <strong>Color_Walls/final.md</strong>: one paragraph sharpened, three shared native illustrations, and a revised closing transition into Patterns after the author deferred Chamber_Color. All other prose and code remain.</p><nav><a href="#encounter">The office</a><a href="#paths">Two colour routes</a><a href="#comparison">What changed</a><a href="#reading">Read the chapter</a><a href="#evidence">Evidence</a><a href="/compose/sources?map=Color_Walls&amp;doc=final">Read and comment</a></nav>'''
page+='<section id="encounter"><h2>Another view, the same way in</h2>'+image('same-opening','The actual office, from the same camera, before and after GLASS / OPAQUE. The chair becomes hidden. The entrance, furniture and every pane collider remain in place.')+'<p>The office can admit your view while refusing your body’s direct approach. Changing opacity interrupts that view. It also gives the person inside a different relation to the aisle, while leaving the way out unchanged.</p><details><summary>Look back from inside the cubicle</summary>'+image('from-the-desk','Both views come from the position reached by the ordinary museum walker plus eye height. The body entered and returned through the same opening in both modes. These are selected views, not headset captures.')+'</details></section>'
page+='<section id="paths"><h2>A colour can have more than one route</h2>'+image('colour-coordinates','The existing RGB cube and HSV cylinder. Each shows five hundred samples. One assigns channels to straight axes; the other places hue around an axis, saturation outward and value upward.')+image('same-endpoints','The existing sixteen-cube comparison, with red and blue held as endpoints. The mode changes the computed interior; no cube moves.')+'<p>The chapter moves from the route through a room to a route between values. The shared endpoints do not settle what lies between them. Both small comparisons remain beside the full-size office.</p></section>'
page+='<section id="comparison"><h2>Keep the question with this wall</h2><p>The revised paragraph follows visibility in both directions and what an opaque partition can provide. It replaces a general request for another doorway with the particular relation already available here. The opening, controls, technical explanations, all three artifacts remain. The closing transition now leads into Pattern_Disco; Chamber_Color has been removed from the active sequence at the author’s request.</p><div class="pair"><div><h3>Before</h3>'+render(revision['old_paragraph'])+'</div><div><h3>Now</h3>'+render(revision['new_paragraph'])+'</div></div><p>The three native illustrations now appear in the canonical chapter. No room or interaction was rebuilt.</p><p><a href="Color_Walls.diff">Exact manuscript diff</a> · <a href="source-changes.diff">Companion evidence notes</a></p></section>'
page+='<section id="reading"><article class="reading">'+render(after)+'</article></section>'
page+='''<section id="evidence" class="evidence"><h2>What was checked</h2><p>43 focused assertions pass in the isolated production museum. Supplied pointer events operate the actual GLASS / OPAQUE button. Supplied keys drive the ordinary controller toward a pane, where it is stopped, then through the neighbouring entrance and back in both modes. This is one cubicle’s route; the earlier all-entrance shape sweeps remain separate, dated evidence.</p><p>All forty pane transforms and exact collision bodies remain unchanged across both toggles, and the original colours return. Eight desks and both five-hundred-sample models remain. RGB sample positions correspond to their stored channels; the black corner’s visibility adjustment is retained.</p><p>The real interpolation button switches from RGB to HSV while keeping the red/blue endpoints. The middle changes, every cube transform stays fixed, and cycling the endpoint buttons and mode returns the original gradient. The chapter’s code excerpts are preserved.</p><p>The first office camera looked mainly through the doorway. A camera-only correction makes the chair’s disappearance behind a pane visible. The final run and final native captures are preserved together; no production repair was needed.</p><p>No map, artifact source, primary selection or control changed. No tracked-controller reach, headset comfort, colour-calibration, learner or performance claim; no live restart, live bake/save overwrite, commit or frozen book/audio rebuild.</p><p><a href="report.json">Runtime record</a> · <a href="source_manifest.json">Capture inputs</a> · <a href="verification.json">Preservation and publication checks</a> · <a href="SUMMARY.md">Findings and decisions</a></p></section><footer>Next: Pattern_Disco — the familiar floor returns in colour.</footer></main></body></html>'''
(O/'index.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
diffs=[]
for rel in json.loads((O/'baseline-hashes.json').read_text()):
 if rel.endswith('/final.md'):continue
 diffs.extend(difflib.unified_diff((O/'before'/rel).read_text(encoding='utf-8').splitlines(True),(R/rel).read_text(encoding='utf-8').splitlines(True),fromfile='before/'+rel,tofile=rel))
(O/'source-changes.diff').write_text(''.join(diffs),encoding='utf-8')
print('Built office encounter, colour comparisons, exact revision and current reading.')
